# Browser
# Stingcaster Mage's trigger gives the Lightning Bolt in Bot1's graveyard flashback until end of turn (CR 702.34a). The
# graveyard pile is lit, its note says which card can be cast and what becomes of it - "Castable this turn, then exiled"
# - and the Bolt says so over its art once the graveyard is open. Cast from there it goes on the stack, the pile is
# dark again (the driver shuts the graveyard it opened), and the Bolt is exiled as it leaves the stack.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Lightning Bolt
Stingcaster Mage
Forest x3
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Graveyard.Lit = false
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Stingcaster Mage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Graveyard.Lit = true
? Client.Bot1.Graveyard.Note = A card here can be cast (Lightning Bolt: Castable this turn, then exiled). Click to look.
? Client.Bot1.Graveyard.Lightning Bolt.Annotation = Castable this turn, then exiled
Bot1.Graveyard.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
? Client.Bot1.Stack = Lightning Bolt
? Client.Bot1.Graveyard.Lit = false
? Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Attack(Stingcaster Mage > Bot2)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 12
Exile = Lightning Bolt
